+# Writing agents and background Posts CSV — lane handoff
+
+This is **partial source implementation**, not installed functionality or legacy parity.
+No migration, browser, worker, real MCP, live provider or production evidence.
+
+Owned files:
+- `agents/config.ts`, `copy.ts`, `manifest.ts`, `mcp.ts`
+- `agents/server/{schema.sql,service.ts,http.ts,copy.ts}`
+- `agents/ui/AgentsScreen.tsx`
+- `publishing/server/export/{config.ts,schema.sql,jobs.ts,entry-points.ts}`
+- `tests/{agents-service,async-post-export}.test.ts`
+
+## Integration outside lane ownership
+
+1. Add the agents manifest to the installed product module list; aggregate
+   `AGENTS_CONFIG`, `AGENT_COPY_CONFIG`, `ASYNC_POST_EXPORT_CONFIG` in installed
+   config and both MCP groups in the installed MCP list. Integrator alone bumps
+   `CONFIG_SCHEMA_VERSION`. New keys: `agents.policy`, `agents.copy`,
+   `publishing.asyncExportPolicy`.
+2. Wrap both schema.sql files in versioned migrations; add their workspace-owned
+   tables to export/erasure/purge and backup coverage before enabling.
+3. Add authenticated thin `/agents` page and `/api/agents` routes. The page loads
+   `writingAgents(actor,{action:'list'})` and `agentCopy(locale)` server-side.
+   Its server action calls the same service with an authenticated actor, never
+   caller-supplied workspace/user ids. Map Zod failures and OperationError through
+   the existing bilingual safe HTTP/action error boundary.
+4. Install a thin Publishing export-job REST route and UI using
+   `postExportAction`; downloads must retain authenticated scope checks and
+   private/no-store headers. Register both MCP groups with independent credential
+   ceilings. MCP transport output byte limits still apply to CSV responses;
+   a private authenticated download route is preferable for large artifacts.
+5. Register worker invocation of `runPostExportJob` and `expirePostExports`.
+   Configure the lease above the existing export transaction timeout. Generation
+   uses the existing RepeatableRead CSV exporter and its Root row/byte/batch caps;
+   it moves work off HTTP but is not a streaming unlimited export. The artifact
+   is stored in PostgreSQL and should move to private streamed storage for very
+   large exports. No silent truncation. A lost lease never overwrites a newer run.
+6. Extend feature/entitlement/navigation/branding declarations for the new Agents
+   module; its present service deliberately uses the existing Posts grant.
+
+## Known unfinished behavior
+
+- Agent draft calls existing metered `runAssist` as an improve request with brief,
+  voice, kind and supplied material encoded as JSON. This preserves provider
+  limits and audit but does **not** establish instructions/voice semantics: the
+  shared AI prompt treats all this as material. AI owner should add a metered
+  agent-draft operation with separately quoted brief/voice/context and reply
+  framing. Do not call this complete post/reply generation parity.
+- Legacy weekly scheduling, timezone-day claims, run history and persisted draft
+  creation are not implemented. No autonomous execution is advertised.
+- Service has update/delete, but the initial screen only creates and generates;
+  editing/removal UI and explicit user confirmation dialogs remain open.
+- Service error messages need an EN/FR Root catalog; screen labels and generic
+  failure are bilingual through `agents.copy` but this is not full localization.
+- Fresh authorization checks are present, but role/entitlement changes racing a
+  transaction require the shared locked authorization pattern before release.
+- Export worker scope is checked before/after generation and on retrieval.
+  Durable export job run history, completion/download audits, retry policy and
+  execution diagnostics remain open. Expiry cleanup must be registered.
+
+## UI skill application
+
+AgentsScreen: taste-skill app-screen rules retain existing module identity and
+content hierarchy; web-design-guidelines uses visible native labels, announced
+busy/error/result states and retained form input. Composition patterns use one
+injected action boundary, explicit form sections and no mode boolean props.
+React best practices use transition pending state and local state, with server
+service code imported only as a type. Shared Button and AutoTextarea retain
+established themes/focus and natural document growth. A user sees a brief form,
+a separate suggestion workspace and an explicit review notice. No custom palette,
+provider branding, fabricated metrics or decorative charts. Browser look/fix,
+phone/desktop and theme checks were not run (lane forbids servers).
+
+## Verification
+
+`npx tsc --noEmit -p .`: zero errors.
+`npx vitest run tests/agents-service.test.ts tests/async-post-export.test.ts --cache=false`:
+9 tests passed. Initial cache-enabled invocation passed assertions but failed
+writing Vitest's cache through the external node_modules symlink (EPERM); rerun
+with cache disabled passed. These are small boundary/unit tests, not persistence,
+concurrency, UI, provider or full parity evidence.
